       Copyright © 1991-2026 Unicode, Inc.
       SPDX-License-Identifier: Unicode-3.0

   The prose of this repository describes CLDR (UTS #35 Part 7) in its own words and links to
   it; no text of the LDML specification is copied.

4. Scan codes (Microsoft documentation)

   The informative position table in SPEC.md, Appendix A, lists for each position the "Scan 1
   Make" code given in the public page "About Keyboard Input"
   (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/inputdev/about-keyboard-input, section
   "Scan codes"), the same page the reference specification cites for the Pause sequence.
   Only the code values are used. targets/windows-default-vk.tsv joins that table by key with the
   public page "Virtual-Key Codes"
   (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/inputdev/virtual-key-codes) for the virtual key
   of each key: facts only (key, scan code, VK), no text of either page. Position names are the `code` values of the W3C
   specification "UI Events KeyboardEvent code Values" (https://www.w3.org/TR/uievents-code/).

